cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  EvidenceRoute: Statistical Evaluation and Contextual-Bandit Routing for
  Reliable Enterprise Question Answering
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Carlos Esteban
    family-names: De La Cruz Ribadeneira
    affiliation: Independent research
repository-code: "https://github.com/tabers77/evidence-route"
abstract: >-
  EvidenceRoute investigates whether a learned decision policy can determine
  when an enterprise question should use lexical retrieval, dense retrieval,
  hybrid retrieval, reranking, an agentic workflow, or abstention — improving
  answer reliability while controlling monetary cost and latency. Candidate
  workflows are executed under a full-information protocol, scored across
  correctness, evidence support, retrieval quality, hallucination risk,
  calibration, cost and latency, and compared using contextual-bandit routing
  and offline policy evaluation with paired uncertainty intervals.
keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - contextual bandits
  - offline policy evaluation
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - LLM evaluation
  - reliable AI
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Evallab (agent-eval): framework-agnostic LLM/agent evaluator"
    notes: >-
      Evaluation and reward layer consumed by EvidenceRoute as a dependency.
    authors:
      - given-names: Carlos Esteban
        family-names: De La Cruz Ribadeneira
